#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133566 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133757 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1fba8401-2da1-50f2-8e96-84cbe06d95fc" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Properties of the Dot Product"}] :question/id #uuid "c374456a-bff7-5145-a590-620bbf50dabf" :question/math-academy-id "e-5536" :question/problem "Find $(5\\mathbf{a}+3\\mathbf{b}) \\cdot \\mathbf{c}+(4\\mathbf{b}+2\\mathbf{c}) \\cdot \\mathbf{d},$ if $\\mathbf{c} \\cdot \\mathbf{a} = 2,$ $\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{c} = -1,$ $\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{d} = 2,$ and $\\mathbf{d} \\cdot \\mathbf{c}=3.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the fact that the dot product is linear in the first variable, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(5a+3b)\\cdot c+(4b+2c)\\cdot d & =(5a)\\cdot c+(3b)\\cdot c+(4b)\\cdot d+(2c)\\cdot d \\\\  & =5(a\\cdot c)+3(b\\cdot c)+4(b\\cdot d)+2(c\\cdot d).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we can substitute the values for $\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{c}$ and $\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{d},$ and use the fact that the dot product is symmetric to get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(a\\cdot c)+3(b\\cdot c)+4(b\\cdot d)+2(c\\cdot d) & =5(c\\cdot a)+3(-1)+4(2)+2(d\\cdot c) \\\\  & =5(c\\cdot a)-3+8+2(d\\cdot c) \\\\  & =5(c\\cdot a)+5+2(d\\cdot c).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the values for $\\mathbf{c} \\cdot \\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{d} \\cdot \\mathbf{c},$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(c\\cdot a)+5+2(d\\cdot c) & =5(2)+5+2(3) \\\\  & =10+5+6 \\\\  & =21.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $(5\\mathbf{a}+3\\mathbf{b}) \\cdot \\mathbf{c}+(4\\mathbf{b}+2\\mathbf{c}) \\cdot \\mathbf{d} = 21.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133567 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133758 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "41c2d289-8df5-551b-9501-3a762c67386f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About the Dot Product"}] :question/id #uuid "13909d3e-b3df-5fcb-9056-5d71283fbebe" :question/math-academy-id "e-5537" :question/problem "Suppose $(4\\mathbf{a} + 2\\mathbf{b}) \\cdot \\mathbf{a} = {0},$ where $\\mathbf{a} \\neq \\mathbf{0}.$ Which of the following statements are true? \n\nI. $\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{a} = -2(\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{a})$\n\nII. $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{a} =  0$\n\nIII. $\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{a} = 1$" :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Simplifying, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4a+2b)\\cdot a & =0 \\\\ (4a)\\cdot a+(2b)\\cdot a & =0 \\\\ 4(a\\cdot a)+2(b\\cdot a) & =0 \\\\ 2(b\\cdot a) & =-4(a\\cdot a) \\\\ b\\cdot a & =-2(a\\cdot a).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\mathbf{a} \\neq \\mathbf{0},$ we must have $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{a} > 0.$\n\n- Statement III is false since it leads to a contradiction. Simplifying $(4\\mathbf{a} + 2\\mathbf{b}) \\cdot \\mathbf{a} = {0}$ and substituting in $\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{a} = 1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4a+2b)\\cdot a & =0 \\\\ 4a\\cdot a+2b\\cdot a & =0 \\\\ 4a\\cdot a+2(1) & =0 \\\\ a\\cdot a & =-\\frac{1}{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nbut this is a contradiction since $\\mathbf{a} \\neq \\mathbf{0}$ implies that $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{a} > 0.$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the correct answer is \"I only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133628 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133813 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "98eb5973-f9b1-5c2f-8763-e8f8707e9b89" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Dot Product"}] :question/id #uuid "7000f188-3223-5a2c-afe6-45fd3f92b8c6" :question/math-academy-id "e-5907" :question/problem "If ![](images/4b/4baf2c746763156bd576054a684a92313185323f40b0dd4c54d4ba29650481aa.svg) ![](images/f1/f1dc50e7cc723ff619fa0ccf3f155c65161a3e6c640385c3b4a5c19f3d66741a.svg) and $\\mathbf{v} \\cdot \\mathbf{v} = 34,$ then what is $\\dfrac{\\mathbf{u}\\cdot 2\\mathbf{v}}{3\\mathbf{v}\\cdot \\mathbf{v}}?$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the fact that the dot product is linear.\n\nTo quickly compute the numerator $\\mathbf{u} \\cdot 2\\mathbf{v},$ we compute $\\mathbf{u} \\cdot \\mathbf{v}$ first and then multiply the result by $2.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot 2v & =2(u\\cdot v) \\\\  & =2({u}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {v}_{4}) \\\\  & =2(7\\cdot 1+5\\cdot 2+(-9)\\cdot (-5)+3\\cdot (-2)) \\\\  & =2(7+10+45-6) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 56 \\\\  & =112.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo quickly compute the denominator $3\\mathbf{v} \\cdot \\mathbf{v},$ we multiply $\\mathbf{v} \\cdot \\mathbf{v}$ by $3.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3v\\cdot v & =3(v\\cdot v) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 34 \\\\  & =102.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\mathbf{u}\\cdot 2\\mathbf{v}}{3\\mathbf{v}\\cdot\\mathbf{v}} =\\dfrac{112}{102}=\\dfrac{56}{51}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186271974 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133757 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1fba8401-2da1-50f2-8e96-84cbe06d95fc" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Properties of the Dot Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30b686da-35fb-5830-8285-acc92ec22f51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269709} {:answer/id #uuid "488eb0f0-077c-5f2d-9556-cfdbe8162354" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-56" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269933} {:answer/id #uuid "5c2ad9f4-81bd-5215-b1fb-5a74ae9a9a7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270089} {:answer/id #uuid "7e5eff5a-9aac-5375-8b40-20061ee9e8a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270373} {:answer/id #uuid "d54e67ec-dd38-5855-9bd5-e3c6b23f5e54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271141}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d54e67ec-dd38-5855-9bd5-e3c6b23f5e54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271141} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c52ac56-104e-5fe0-934f-5eb6c3f2a14f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271786}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "72bce1cb-eaf1-5fbc-a940-e7b74a9a7f59" :question/math-academy-id "q-139951" :question/problem "If $\\alpha \\beta =-8$ and $b\\cdot a=\\frac{15}{2}$, then what is $(\\alpha a)\\cdot (\\beta b)+12?$" :question/worked-solution "Using the fact that the dot product is linear in both variables, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\alpha a)\\cdot (\\beta b)+12 & =\\alpha (a\\cdot \\beta b)+12 \\\\  & =\\alpha \\beta (a\\cdot b)+12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, using that the dot product is symmetric, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\alpha \\beta (a\\cdot b)+12 & =\\alpha \\beta (b\\cdot a)+12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute the values for $\\alpha \\beta $ and $b\\cdot a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\alpha \\beta (b\\cdot a)+12 & =(-8)\\cdot \\frac{15}{2}+12 \\\\  & =-60+12 \\\\  & =-48\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134197 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133813 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "98eb5973-f9b1-5c2f-8763-e8f8707e9b89" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Dot Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b7977a2-7896-5f02-8392-a8a160b6c156" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{15}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131222} {:answer/id #uuid "a3cc2ba7-6d9d-5504-bc7e-709fd733bd40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{22}{75}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131223} {:answer/id #uuid "c9d00e13-409b-58ca-b072-af0e61862a0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{75}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131224} {:answer/id #uuid "3f455e85-79b6-5b83-81ea-b3a19f090e61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{44}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131225} {:answer/id #uuid "4c194db3-28a2-55f6-9353-ac2a12136ec4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{11}{150}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131226}] :answer-field/id #uuid "ce14b266-f04b-5e8e-9812-9e4278e42ef4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131221}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ed79d14a-ab1d-5f6d-90f6-11a9ac5f0180" :question/math-academy-id "q-39195" :question/problem "If $u = \\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}$, $v = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}$, and $u \\cdot v =-22$, then $(u \\cdot (2v))/(u \\cdot (5u)) =$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326749 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133757 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1fba8401-2da1-50f2-8e96-84cbe06d95fc" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Properties of the Dot Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02310999-31d5-55c2-910f-da601b7a00ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323991} {:answer/id #uuid "13b0bd98-37a8-5cf9-8bc7-b32b2855761a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324148} {:answer/id #uuid "67b7ca33-6368-51bd-86b6-ea53a5343745" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324836} {:answer/id #uuid "dee34431-0772-5613-bc26-5a169ac516ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325919} {:answer/id #uuid "eb62aad8-dcd0-5854-915b-c886815fef2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326044}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dee34431-0772-5613-bc26-5a169ac516ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325919} :answer-field/id #uuid "f94f2a72-b3ea-5975-80ac-5c07b3859227" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326664}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "810e998d-a1df-5b30-9fd3-e9a97dd285f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-39196" :question/problem "Find $(2a+5b)\\cdot c+(b+3c)\\cdot d,$ if $c\\cdot a=2,$ $b\\cdot c=3,$ $b\\cdot d=4$ and $d\\cdot c=1.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the fact that the dot product is linear in the first variable, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2a+5b)\\cdot c+(b+3c)\\cdot d & =(2a)\\cdot c+(5b)\\cdot c+b\\cdot d+(3c)\\cdot d \\\\  & =2(a\\cdot c)+5(b\\cdot c)+b\\cdot d+3(c\\cdot d).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we can use the fact that the dot product is symmetric to get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(a\\cdot c)+5(b\\cdot c)+b\\cdot d+3(c\\cdot d) & =2(c\\cdot a)+5(b\\cdot c)+b\\cdot d+3(d\\cdot c).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the values for $c\\cdot a,$ $b\\cdot c,$ $b\\cdot d,$ and $d\\cdot c,$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(c\\cdot a)+5(b\\cdot c)+b\\cdot d+3(d\\cdot c) & =2(2)+5(3)+4+3(1) \\\\  & =4+15+4+3 \\\\  & =26.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $(2a+5b)\\cdot c+(b+3c)\\cdot d=26.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186575577 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133813 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "98eb5973-f9b1-5c2f-8763-e8f8707e9b89" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Dot Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c1e4807-a090-51b6-b8a5-0ed1a73a6532" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{20}{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575022} {:answer/id #uuid "9ba6f34d-ea9c-55cd-ac5e-4ff8b3862bad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{39}{23}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575215} {:answer/id #uuid "a7c0fb46-4c53-5f39-8235-7070192b77ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575244} {:answer/id #uuid "bb1c0734-9ff2-5360-9a7c-45a81e9c5de1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{19}{21}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575283} {:answer/id #uuid "cac76ba4-017f-5e57-8edb-6869b8b020aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{38}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575308}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7c0fb46-4c53-5f39-8235-7070192b77ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575244} :answer-field/id #uuid "5bf3387a-a036-5d98-81f1-318396ac1845" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575456}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "955d6eb2-9fbf-5873-9d9e-5edc1cabeb28" :question/math-academy-id "q-39201" :question/problem "If $u=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\\,,$ $v=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\,,$ and $u\\cdot v=22,$ then $\\frac{(3u)\\cdot v}{u\\cdot (2u)}=$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the fact that the dot product is linear.\n\nTo quickly compute the numerator $3u\\cdot v,$ we multiply $u\\cdot v$ by $3.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3u)\\cdot v & =3(u\\cdot v) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 22 \\\\  & =66.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo quickly compute the denominator $u\\cdot (2u),$ we compute $u\\cdot u$ first and then multiply the result by $2.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot (2u) & =2(u\\cdot u) \\\\  & =2({u}_{1}^{2}+{u}_{2}^{2}+{u}_{3}^{2}+{u}_{4}^{2}) \\\\  & =2({2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{5}^{2}) \\\\  & =2(4+1+9+25) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 39 \\\\  & =78.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{(3u)\\cdot v}{u\\cdot (2u)}=\\frac{66}{78}=\\frac{11}{13}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134200 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133758 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "41c2d289-8df5-551b-9501-3a762c67386f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About the Dot Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab86b64c-6ab4-51d0-bc53-bc2b9d9020a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131240} {:answer/id #uuid "c1f4b457-3b5b-540f-b504-d2b1b0be5aaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131241} {:answer/id #uuid "22b98eaf-eb11-530a-a4a2-6ee7dc4fced2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131242} {:answer/id #uuid "2740dcef-96c4-5ed6-b9d3-0d8287a4b5f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the statements are true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131243} {:answer/id #uuid "33050ae9-151b-5e50-b859-cb75f312ce42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131244}] :answer-field/id #uuid "ee5bfc63-f8e9-5043-929d-af789ad6720e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131239}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "94a31460-c755-5749-ae5b-c94244d2f1ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-39204" :question/problem "Suppose $(9a + 3b) \\cdot a = 0$, where $a \\ne 0$. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $b \\cdot a = 3(a \\cdot a)$\n2. $a \\cdot a < 0$\n3. $b \\cdot a = 1$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186575526 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133758 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "41c2d289-8df5-551b-9501-3a762c67386f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About the Dot Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f7cb973-f85c-5e6b-8dae-6a8ad95726f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575000} {:answer/id #uuid "31e67c9f-c8c0-5b64-be70-6a0f3503ae5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575035} {:answer/id #uuid "a1584f84-f877-5de9-9302-da994b87ba25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575232} {:answer/id #uuid "d73bfa84-e3d5-5e2c-8d3f-8a839c69c8b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575333} {:answer/id #uuid "f67b9fe9-2313-58df-9ac7-22477599208d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575386}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a1584f84-f877-5de9-9302-da994b87ba25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575232} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b8314bc-1ca0-55b2-b63e-52c99907cd1e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575475}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "02eb1a38-d05c-54e9-9813-73779e1c0487" :question/math-academy-id "q-40050" :question/problem "Suppose $(8a+2b)\\cdot a=0$, where $a\\ne 0.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $b\\cdot a=4(a\\cdot a)$\n\nII. $-a\\cdot a<0$\n\nIII. $b\\cdot a=4$" :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Simplifying the expression $(8a+2b)\\cdot a=0$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(8a+2b)\\cdot a & =0 \\\\ (8a)\\cdot a+(2b)\\cdot a & =0 \\\\ 8(a\\cdot a)+2(b\\cdot a) & =0 \\\\ 2(b\\cdot a) & =-8(a\\cdot a) \\\\ b\\cdot a & =-4(a\\cdot a)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $a\\ne 0,$ we must have $a\\cdot a>0$, which implies $-a\\cdot a<0.$\n\n- Statement III is false since it leads to a contradiction. If $b\\cdot a=4$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(8a+2b)\\cdot a & =0 \\\\ 8(a\\cdot a)+2(b\\cdot a) & =0 \\\\ 8(a\\cdot a)+2(4) & =0 \\\\ a\\cdot a & =-1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nbut this is a contradiction since $a\\ne 0$ implies that $a\\cdot a>0.$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186575617 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133757 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1fba8401-2da1-50f2-8e96-84cbe06d95fc" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Properties of the Dot Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20e89a4c-5fb7-5f90-9b49-1d353949f7db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575002} {:answer/id #uuid "2bc45b67-7aab-542f-93de-d964f0d1ff29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{13}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575020} {:answer/id #uuid "52f9c109-ae8a-59e7-8c53-96071e29be14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575094} {:answer/id #uuid "8677ef66-ef3c-5e2c-a8ae-ea47b6b8232d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575186} {:answer/id #uuid "9a3b1762-1f3b-5c50-bdd6-fd9a76ca82e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575212}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9a3b1762-1f3b-5c50-bdd6-fd9a76ca82e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575212} :answer-field/id #uuid "442c71b0-f1e1-596b-a7c5-af88038d1f0b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575449}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ebc01d60-f520-5118-a5cd-4a61bccfbcb3" :question/math-academy-id "q-40051" :question/problem "Suppose ${b}_{2}=p{b}_{1}+a$ and ${b}_{1}\\cdot {b}_{2}=0.$ If $a=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$ and ${b}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}$, find the value of $p.$ \n\n*Hint: You might wish to take the equation ${b}_{2}=p{b}_{1}+a$ and find the dot product of both sides with ${b}_{1}.$*" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the equation ${b}_{2}=p{b}_{1}+a$ and find the dot product of both sides with ${b}_{1}$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{2} & =p{b}_{1}+a \\\\ {b}_{1}\\cdot {b}_{2} & ={b}_{1}\\cdot (p{b}_{1}+a) \\\\ {b}_{1}\\cdot {b}_{2} & ={b}_{1}\\cdot (p{b}_{1})+({b}_{1}\\cdot a) \\\\ {b}_{1}\\cdot {b}_{2} & =p({b}_{1}\\cdot {b}_{1})+({b}_{1}\\cdot a)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the formula for the dot product to compute the values of ${b}_{1}\\cdot {b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{1}\\cdot a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1}\\cdot {b}_{1} & ={b}_{1}^{2}+{b}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & ={2}^{2}+(-3)^{2} \\\\  & =4+9 \\\\  & =13 \\\\ {b}_{1}\\cdot a & ={b}_{1}{a}_{1}+{b}_{2}{a}_{2} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 2+(-3)\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =4+3 \\\\  & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the values for ${b}_{1}\\cdot {b}_{1},$ ${b}_{1}\\cdot a,$ and ${b}_{1}\\cdot {b}_{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1}\\cdot {b}_{2} & =p({b}_{1}\\cdot {b}_{1})+({b}_{1}\\cdot a) \\\\ 0 & =p\\cdot 13+7 \\\\ -13p & =7 \\\\ p & =-\\frac{7}{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326807 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133813 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "98eb5973-f9b1-5c2f-8763-e8f8707e9b89" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Dot Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "527943b8-7e4d-5502-a5f2-f8ba6fe56dcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324644} {:answer/id #uuid "6dffc1cf-e64f-514b-be69-bdbf983d37b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324876} {:answer/id #uuid "7754a4fc-07b1-5762-ac28-0fd1afa04900" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{16}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324962} {:answer/id #uuid "a9ea1716-1cba-522a-a907-a9c1d41ab36b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325417} {:answer/id #uuid "c4c45d32-4fc7-523d-bf51-e0a2a256b628" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{17}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325664}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4c45d32-4fc7-523d-bf51-e0a2a256b628" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{17}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325664} :answer-field/id #uuid "edda396f-e742-5019-a534-258da355df7e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326648}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8894591e-36c3-50df-8b05-4273bf54c4d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-40108" :question/problem "If $u=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\,,$ $v=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}\\,,$ and $u\\cdot u=17,$ then $\\frac{u\\cdot (2u)}{u\\cdot (\\frac{1}{3}v)}=$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the fact that the dot product is linear.\n\nTo quickly compute the numerator $u\\cdot (2u),$ we multiply $u\\cdot u$ by $2.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot (2u) & =2(u\\cdot u) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 17 \\\\  & =34.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo quickly compute the denominator $u\\cdot (\\frac{1}{3}v),$ we compute $u\\cdot v$ first and then multiply the result by $\\frac{1}{3}.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot (\\frac{1}{3}v) & =\\frac{1}{3}({u}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {v}_{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}((0)\\cdot (1)+3\\cdot (-4)+2\\cdot 2+2\\cdot (-5)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(0-12+4-10) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (-18) \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{u\\cdot (2u)}{u\\cdot (\\frac{1}{3}v)}=\\frac{34}{-6}=-\\frac{17}{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186575554 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133757 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1fba8401-2da1-50f2-8e96-84cbe06d95fc" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Properties of the Dot Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03c5dd2d-fff5-5991-b111-3e6faa486a85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574958} {:answer/id #uuid "7cadc3ff-14b7-5d0c-a857-04adb0277a4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "69" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575175} {:answer/id #uuid "7e617142-bdf7-5c0b-95cf-0477f897470a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-123" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575177} {:answer/id #uuid "a7be4d76-3b4f-5c13-acc0-14a057882597" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575243} {:answer/id #uuid "fe9bc857-346c-500f-b144-1a055df9866b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575405}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7be4d76-3b4f-5c13-acc0-14a057882597" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575243} :answer-field/id #uuid "c86deb60-271b-56a0-b579-07d9a6af8966" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575498}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "64386ab8-01dd-5ca3-af09-05de11ca4efa" :question/math-academy-id "q-40114" :question/problem "If $\\alpha \\beta =12$ and $a\\cdot b=4$, then what is $(\\alpha b)\\cdot (\\beta a)-21?$" :question/worked-solution "Using the fact that the dot product is linear in both variables, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\alpha b)\\cdot (\\beta a)-21 & =\\alpha (b\\cdot \\beta a)-21 \\\\  & =\\alpha \\beta (b\\cdot a)-21.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, using that the dot product is symmetric, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\alpha \\beta (b\\cdot a)-21 & =\\alpha \\beta (a\\cdot b)-21.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute the values for $\\alpha \\beta$ and $a\\cdot b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\alpha \\beta (a\\cdot b)-21 & =12\\cdot (4)-21 \\\\  & =48-21 \\\\  & =27\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326808 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133758 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "41c2d289-8df5-551b-9501-3a762c67386f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About the Dot Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e1db8eb7-e09f-56da-a287-35714cc28cf2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467458} {:answer/id #uuid "b1ff2546-2a88-5435-acbe-93df7f7eeafd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467459}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b1ff2546-2a88-5435-acbe-93df7f7eeafd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467459} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba8eda63-91b1-56f5-a4df-cc1f8bc6d99c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468450} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e828117-5723-519f-b893-5316f2b3b3b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467460} {:answer/id #uuid "c561fe9a-88e5-52b1-bde8-e459bbebb99e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467461}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1e828117-5723-519f-b893-5316f2b3b3b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467460} :answer-field/id #uuid "45d4bccf-e659-550b-b666-e63b0610397f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468451} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "721e29c5-37a8-527b-a2c2-c18d8874306e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467462} {:answer/id #uuid "9be70914-f2ac-53e2-9d6c-276ded2ea1b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467463}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "721e29c5-37a8-527b-a2c2-c18d8874306e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467462} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b258030-52f1-5a01-ae8e-9fcee2a439b4" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468452}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b1453d9c-0156-5211-9ae1-5e44ccac6939" :question/math-academy-id "q-40116" :question/problem "Suppose $(6a-9b)\\cdot a=0$, where $a\\ne 0.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $a\\cdot a>0$\n\n- **II.** $a\\cdot a=\\frac{1}{2}(b\\cdot a)$\n\n- **III.** $b\\cdot a=-4$" :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indedd, $a\\ne 0$ implies that $a\\cdot a>0.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Simplifying the expression $(6a-9b)\\cdot a=0$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(6a-9b)\\cdot a & =0 \\\\ (6a)\\cdot a-(9b)\\cdot a & =0 \\\\ 6(a\\cdot a)-9(b\\cdot a) & =0 \\\\ 6(a\\cdot a) & =9(b\\cdot a) \\\\ a\\cdot a & =\\frac{3}{2}(b\\cdot a)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false since it leads to a contradiction. If $b\\cdot a=-4$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(6a-9b)\\cdot a & =0 \\\\ 6(a\\cdot a)-9(b\\cdot a) & =0 \\\\ 6(a\\cdot a)-9(-4) & =0 \\\\ a\\cdot a & =-6,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nbut this is a contradiction since $a\\ne 0$ implies that $a\\cdot a>0.$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the correct answer is \"I only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186575548 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133757 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1fba8401-2da1-50f2-8e96-84cbe06d95fc" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Properties of the Dot Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01b2add6-2c67-53b2-8c90-f94f33352bd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574954} {:answer/id #uuid "2e0d5123-afe9-526f-8c30-e9359cc8929b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575024} {:answer/id #uuid "588d46c7-6540-5faa-af52-4cc4aba10d7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575105} {:answer/id #uuid "5b99a9cb-3ede-545e-b81d-553fa9eb7060" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575112} {:answer/id #uuid "fac7fb28-675a-5240-a386-a6c076509e51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575396}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01b2add6-2c67-53b2-8c90-f94f33352bd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574954} :answer-field/id #uuid "05042bcd-7408-5162-a150-fc8ad84cb0bf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575409}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5a4c9f12-f1ec-53fb-81d9-ded6a93d72ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-40121" :question/problem "Suppose ${b}_{2}=k{b}_{1}-a$ and ${b}_{1}\\cdot {b}_{2}=0.$ If $a=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$ and ${b}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$, find the value of $k.$ \n\n*Hint: You might wish to take the equation ${b}_{2}=k{b}_{1}-a$ and find the dot product of both sides with ${b}_{1}.$*" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the equation ${b}_{2}=k{b}_{1}-a$ and find the dot product of both sides with ${b}_{1}$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{2} & =k{b}_{1}-a \\\\ {b}_{1}\\cdot {b}_{2} & ={b}_{1}\\cdot (k{b}_{1}-a) \\\\ {b}_{1}\\cdot {b}_{2} & ={b}_{1}\\cdot (k{b}_{1})-({b}_{1}\\cdot a) \\\\ {b}_{1}\\cdot {b}_{2} & =k({b}_{1}\\cdot {b}_{1})-({b}_{1}\\cdot a)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the formula for the dot product to compute the values of ${b}_{1}\\cdot {b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{1}\\cdot a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1}\\cdot {b}_{1} & ={b}_{1}^{2}+{b}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & ={2}^{2}+{0}^{2} \\\\  & =4 \\\\ {b}_{1}\\cdot a & ={b}_{1}{a}_{1}+{b}_{2}{a}_{2} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 1+0\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the values for ${b}_{1}\\cdot {b}_{1},$ ${b}_{1}\\cdot a,$ and ${b}_{1}\\cdot {b}_{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1}\\cdot {b}_{2} & =k({b}_{1}\\cdot {b}_{1})-({b}_{1}\\cdot a) \\\\ 0 & =k\\cdot 4-2 \\\\ -4k & =-2 \\\\ k & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186575550 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133813 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "98eb5973-f9b1-5c2f-8763-e8f8707e9b89" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Dot Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "380840fb-2296-517d-ad92-c6d825c59d64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575043} {:answer/id #uuid "54efae19-05c8-5b57-963e-300afde1484a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575097} {:answer/id #uuid "71ea6c44-df5f-5252-9451-daec1e4b3af2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{10}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575157} {:answer/id #uuid "83f122af-a146-53a7-835c-5b286f8e1460" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{22}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575185} {:answer/id #uuid "e938bc27-9cfe-54d8-86d0-a5645cd5bfdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575362}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "380840fb-2296-517d-ad92-c6d825c59d64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575043} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea8e249e-3dee-5215-9e54-0f6bd4c6007a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575518}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "61c2f333-f089-53c4-9125-104e2258d303" :question/math-academy-id "q-74038" :question/problem "If $u=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\,,$ $v=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\,,$ and $u\\cdot v=-2,$ then $\\frac{u\\cdot (10v)}{u\\cdot (4u)}=$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the fact that the dot product is linear.\n\nTo quickly compute the numerator $u\\cdot (10v),$ we multiply $u\\cdot v$ by $10.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot (10v) & =10(u\\cdot v) \\\\  & =10\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo quickly compute the denominator $u\\cdot (4u),$ we compute $u\\cdot u$ first and then multiply the result by $4.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot (4u) & =4(u\\cdot u) \\\\  & =4({u}_{1}^{2}+{u}_{2}^{2}+{u}_{3}^{2}+{u}_{4}^{2}) \\\\  & =4((-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+(-1)^{2}) \\\\  & =4(1+4+1+4+1) \\\\  & =4\\cdot 11 \\\\  & =44.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{u\\cdot (10v)}{u\\cdot (4u)}=\\frac{-20}{44}=-\\frac{5}{11}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342136 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133813 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "98eb5973-f9b1-5c2f-8763-e8f8707e9b89" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Dot Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66f8b296-106a-55d1-a158-baf48d60df5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340034} {:answer/id #uuid "68d35a3f-876f-54f1-9c6d-6842edcacf33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{27}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340061} {:answer/id #uuid "8646d07a-d818-586f-811d-6c97d5448210" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "54" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340332} {:answer/id #uuid "f27c5c33-e7f4-5731-a888-81756735387b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341264} {:answer/id #uuid "f50488aa-44f3-5c4f-abb6-198bf43e1efc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{18}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341289}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f50488aa-44f3-5c4f-abb6-198bf43e1efc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{18}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341289} :answer-field/id #uuid "829e24de-c424-53e1-bc03-8eea86703998" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341610}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "47c69ee1-f7fb-57b5-8f21-3fbf9a1f0073" :question/math-academy-id "q-74040" :question/problem "If $u=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\\,,$ $v=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\,,$ and $u\\cdot u=27,$ then $\\frac{(2u)\\cdot u}{u\\cdot (3v)}=$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the fact that the dot product is linear.\n\nTo quickly compute the numerator $(2u)\\cdot u,$ we multiply $u\\cdot u$ by $2.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2u)\\cdot u & =2(u\\cdot u) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 27 \\\\  & =54.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo quickly compute the denominator $u\\cdot (3v),$ we compute $u\\cdot v$ first and then multiply the result by $3.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot (3v) & =3(u\\cdot v) \\\\  & =3({u}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {v}_{4}) \\\\  & =3(2\\cdot (-3)+3\\cdot (-2)+1\\cdot (-1)+(-2)\\cdot 3+(-3)\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =3(-6-6-1-6-6) \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-25) \\\\  & =-75.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{(2u)\\cdot u}{u\\cdot (3v)}=\\frac{54}{-75}=-\\frac{18}{25}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342139 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133758 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "41c2d289-8df5-551b-9501-3a762c67386f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About the Dot Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d0b1c4a0-5efb-57ea-afe1-d4dc0d263d3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451615} {:answer/id #uuid "aea40534-564b-5041-9106-8f422cba5401" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451616}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0b1c4a0-5efb-57ea-afe1-d4dc0d263d3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451615} :answer-field/id #uuid "17efcf99-d195-5449-b270-dd763616532f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452655} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "298b65b7-d917-54c3-8430-6e1c198fd17f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451617} {:answer/id #uuid "843c4f82-ee34-5415-8ec5-3eb2c9d21dd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451618}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "298b65b7-d917-54c3-8430-6e1c198fd17f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451617} :answer-field/id #uuid "dcb97538-a4a6-59cb-ba0c-18441a2d3fcd" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452656} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "100f83a6-d105-585a-835c-7c9b9b59b8c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451619} {:answer/id #uuid "a78b485d-bb5b-5f50-9378-ad835cb44037" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451620}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a78b485d-bb5b-5f50-9378-ad835cb44037" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451620} :answer-field/id #uuid "2337796b-4d0f-559b-8850-eb51b2d663f4" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452657}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ec2dfaf1-eafb-5d88-8d0f-be9d2909829b" :question/math-academy-id "q-74049" :question/problem "Suppose $(a+b)\\cdot a=0$, where $a\\ne 0.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $a\\cdot a<0$\n- **II.** $b\\cdot a=a\\cdot a$\n- **III.** $b\\cdot a<0$" :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since $a\\ne 0$, we must have $a\\cdot a>0.$\n\n- Statement II is false while statement III is true. Simplifying the expression $(a+b)\\cdot a=0$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(a+b)\\cdot a & =0 \\\\ a\\cdot a+b\\cdot a & =0 \\\\ b\\cdot a & =-a\\cdot a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nSince $a\\ne 0$ implies that $a\\cdot a>0$, we obtain that $-a\\cdot a<0.$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the correct answer is \"III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186575604 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133758 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "41c2d289-8df5-551b-9501-3a762c67386f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About the Dot Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43183136-6c70-5fb6-9cb4-2acf917b14f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575066} {:answer/id #uuid "66cc3909-10ef-593c-8821-e7238b004d27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575134} {:answer/id #uuid "7699f0ee-def5-536a-a004-b4578f68883e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575166} {:answer/id #uuid "9d62eb9a-b60d-5fcb-8454-b577309849b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575219} {:answer/id #uuid "b16177cb-e181-5c27-9326-9ecb9a4963bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575265}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "66cc3909-10ef-593c-8821-e7238b004d27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575134} :answer-field/id #uuid "415ea050-0cd5-5d54-b8f3-6177bceb1f0d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575446}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d0f13f7c-58e9-5582-87a9-733c8480e4b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-74050" :question/problem "Suppose $(a+b)\\cdot a=0$, where $a\\ne 0.$ Which of the following statements are true? \n\nI. $b\\cdot a<0$\n\nII. $b\\cdot a=3$\n\nIII. $a\\cdot a=-3$" :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true while statement II is false. Simplifying the expression $(a+b)\\cdot a=0$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(a+b)\\cdot a & =0 \\\\ a\\cdot a+b\\cdot a & =0 \\\\ b\\cdot a & =-a\\cdot a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nSince $a\\ne 0$ implies that $a\\cdot a>0$, we obtain that $-a\\cdot a<0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $a\\ne 0,$ we must have $a\\cdot a>0.$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the correct answer is \"I only.\""}]}
